    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "it just feels so exhausting. like i'm just performing being a person because i feel like i'm supposed to. but there's no reward at the end of any of this. everything that gave my life meaning is just... gone. and now i'm just stuck in this loop of existing for no reason. it's like i'm waiting for something to happen, but nothing ever will.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "That feeling of performing a life without inherent reward is a heavy burden to carry during the winter of grief. It can seem as though the grief itself has stolen your agency, leaving you feeling like a passenger in a life you cannot drive. Please be gentle with yourself on these hard days; healing isn't a straight line, and there is no single timeline for finding meaning again.\n</think>",
      "source": "target",
